"900.3.10(57)":{"explanation":"Exception RD 57 switches off the building length and building depth regulations on these lands, and the former City of North York by-law 30540 and the Schedule 'D' Airport Hazard Map of North York by-law 7625 continue to apply as prevailing instruments.","code_refs":"none"},
"900.3.10(287)":{"explanation":"Exception RD 287 sets the minimum lot frontage and lot area at what existed on the day By-law 569-2013 was enacted, a 0.9 m minimum side setback, a 3.6 m minimum setback from a side lot line abutting a street, and allows the part of a building with a parking space in a side yard if it is at least 0.3 m from the side lot line.","code_refs":"none"},
"900.3.10(245)":{"explanation":"Exception RD 245 sets the minimum lot frontage and lot area at what existed on the date By-law 569-2013 was enacted, a 40 percent maximum lot coverage for all buildings, a 1.2 m minimum side yard setback, a 5.7 m minimum setback from a side lot line abutting a street, and a 0.3 m minimum setback for an attached or detached garage from a side lot line that does not abut a street.","code_refs":"none"},
"900.3.10(562)":{"explanation":"Exception RD 562 sets the minimum lot frontage and lot area at what existed on the day By-law 569-2013 was enacted, a 1.2 m minimum side setback, a 0.3 m minimum setback for an attached garage from a side lot line that does not abut a street, a 4.5 m minimum setback from a side lot line abutting a street, and requires the required parking space to be located in the residential building.","code_refs":"none"}
}}
